cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Replication package for "Cluster-Aware Uncertainty for Polytomous Mokken
  Scalability: A Calibrated Hierarchical Bayesian Bootstrap"
message: >-
  If you use this package, please cite both it and the article it accompanies.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/joonho112/bayesmokken-clustered-polytomous-replication
url: https://joonho112.github.io/bayesmokken-clustered-polytomous-replication/
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: JoonHo
    email: jlee296@ua.edu
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-4019-8703
    affiliation: The University of Alabama
abstract: >-
  Rebuilds every number, figure and table in Lee (2026) from a frozen analysis
  snapshot spanning a feasibility pilot, a training and held-out validation
  split, a fresh 24-cell confirmation at 6,400 replications per population
  target, and an application to the SWMDK data distributed with the mokken
  package. Ships the complete raw draw streams of the application (12 tasks of
  99,999 draws), the 86,400 raw confirmation replication rows, the hash-locked
  protocol and receipt files, an annotated reference copy of the pipeline, and
  an independent oracle lane that checks finite comonotone transport against a
  linear-programming solution and reproduces the published results of Koopman
  et al. (2022).
keywords:
  - Mokken scale analysis
  - polytomous scalability
  - clustered data
  - hierarchical Bayesian bootstrap
  - comonotone transport
  - confidence interval
  - reproducibility
  - replication package
